WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.947
A web address should be short and readable.

00:00:03.947 --> 00:00:09.060
The Autoroute module gives a content item a permalink, generated from a pattern

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.105
that usually uses the title.

00:00:11.105 --> 00:00:17.300
In this video, you attach Autoroute to a content type, choose its options, and manage permalinks.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:26.968
Without Autoroute, Orchard Core displays a content item at an address that ends

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:31.440
with the identifier of the item, a long string of letters and digits.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.720
Visitors can't read it, remember it, or guess it.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.664
A content type, such as Event, is made of parts, and Autoroute is

00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:41.732
a part that you attach to it.

00:00:41.732 --> 00:00:45.868
Each saved item then receives a permalink, built from a pattern.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:50.830
By default, the pattern turns the title into lowercase words joined by dashes.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:59.295
The Autoroute part comes from a feature, listed under Tools, Features.

00:00:59.295 --> 00:01:00.800
Search for Autoroute:

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.425
it's enabled here, because the Blog recipe that set up this site turns it on.

00:01:05.425 --> 00:01:07.710
On another site, you select Enable.

00:01:08.184 --> 00:01:11.633
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types.

00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:16.774
Choose Edit on Event, a type that has a Title part and no Autoroute part.

00:01:17.231 --> 00:01:19.641
The Parts list shows what the type contains.

00:01:19.641 --> 00:01:22.821
Choose Add Parts to see the parts that you can attach to it.

00:01:23.275 --> 00:01:28.464
Autoroute is on the list, described as providing a custom URL for your content item.

00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:30.771
Choose Add & Configure on its row.

00:01:30.771 --> 00:01:35.325
Orchard Core attaches the part to the Event type, and opens its settings.

00:01:39.587 --> 00:01:42.962
This page holds the Autoroute settings of the Event type.

00:01:42.962 --> 00:01:48.587
The Pattern field contains the template that builds each permalink, and its default uses the title.

00:01:48.587 --> 00:01:51.587
A separate video covers writing your own patterns.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.340
Let's turn on Allow custom path.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.173
It lets editors type their own permalink.

00:01:57.173 --> 00:02:02.900
When it stays off, the Permalink field can't be edited, and every permalink is generated.

00:02:03.354 --> 00:02:05.512
Let's turn on Allow path updates.

00:02:05.512 --> 00:02:09.219
It adds a Refresh the path option to the editor, for when the

00:02:09.219 --> 00:02:10.934
title of an item changes.

00:02:11.386 --> 00:02:13.817
Let's turn on Show homepage options.

00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:17.696
It adds Set as homepage to the editor, for users who have the

00:02:17.696 --> 00:02:19.837
permission to set the homepage.

00:02:19.837 --> 00:02:22.326
A separate video covers the homepage.

00:02:22.782 --> 00:02:24.709
Let's turn on Allow disabled.

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:29.722
It adds a Disabled option to the editor, which turns Autoroute off for a single item.

00:02:30.186 --> 00:02:35.180
Container Settings, further down, are for items that contain other items and for

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.839
the items they contain, such as a taxonomy and its terms.

00:02:38.839 --> 00:02:42.206
Let's leave them as they are, and save the settings.

00:02:46.396 --> 00:02:51.596
Under Content, Content Items, the New button lists the content types that you can create.

00:02:51.596 --> 00:02:52.636
Choose Event.

00:02:53.095 --> 00:02:55.932
Enter the title, Spring Planting Workshop.

00:02:55.932 --> 00:03:00.306
The Permalink field stays empty, and its hint says to leave it empty

00:03:00.306 --> 00:03:02.198
to generate the permalink.

00:03:02.198 --> 00:03:05.863
The options that these settings add are on the form too:

00:03:05.863 --> 00:03:09.055
Disabled, Set as homepage, and Refresh the path.

00:03:09.506 --> 00:03:10.705
Select Publish.

00:03:10.705 --> 00:03:16.015
Autoroute generates the permalink from the title, in lowercase, with dashes between the

00:03:16.015 --> 00:03:20.241
words, and adds a dash and a number if another item already uses it.

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:22.296
The event appears in the list.

00:03:22.755 --> 00:03:25.147
Choose Edit to open the item again.

00:03:25.147 --> 00:03:31.155
The Permalink field shows the generated permalink, and a link beside it opens the published page.

00:03:31.612 --> 00:03:32.789
Follow the link.

00:03:32.789 --> 00:03:36.803
The page is displayed at an address that ends with the permalink, and

00:03:36.803 --> 00:03:38.622
no identifier appears in it.

00:03:42.828 --> 00:03:48.065
In Content Items, let's open the event again, and change its title to Spring Planting Day.

00:03:48.065 --> 00:03:52.048
The Permalink field holds the permalink built from the first title.

00:03:52.525 --> 00:03:54.785
Publish, and open the item again.

00:03:54.785 --> 00:03:58.437
The Permalink field holds the first permalink, unchanged.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:03.306
Autoroute generates a permalink only when the field is empty, so the addresses

00:04:03.306 --> 00:04:05.915
that visitors already use keep working.

00:04:06.405 --> 00:04:09.249
To follow the title, turn on Refresh the path.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:13.133
Its hint warns that the previous URL won't be accessible anymore.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.665
Then publish the item.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.709
Open the item once more.

00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:21.530
The Permalink field holds the permalink generated from the title Spring Planting Day.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.570
You can also type your own permalink.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:29.610
Orchard Core refuses one that another item already uses, and one that contains

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.710
a space, and it explains why.

00:04:32.202 --> 00:04:34.920
Replace the space with a dash, and publish.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.194
Orchard Core accepts the permalink.

00:04:37.194 --> 00:04:38.581
Then open the item:

00:04:38.581 --> 00:04:41.632
the Permalink field holds exactly what you typed.

00:04:43.632 --> 00:04:45.596
That's the Autoroute module:

00:04:45.596 --> 00:04:51.490
readable, unique permalinks for your content items, with options that each content type decides.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.992
Thanks for watching.

